Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Statement I:</strong></td><td><span id="cke_bm_1255S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>The time period of revolution of an electron in its <span class="math-tex">\(n^\mathrm{th}\)</span> Bohr orbit in an atom is directly proportional to <span class="math-tex">\(n^3.\)</span></td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td><span id="cke_bm_1635S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>The kinetic energy of an electron in its <span class="math-tex">\(n^\mathrm{th}\)</span> Bohr orbit in an atom is directly proportional to <span class="math-tex">\(n.\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 6%;">1.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect and <strong>Statement II</strong> is correct.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">2.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I</strong> and <strong>Statement II</strong> are correct.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">3.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I</strong> and <strong>Statement II</strong> are incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 6%;">4.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct and <strong>Statement II</strong> is incorrect.</td></tr></tbody></table>
